# Media Handling Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines establish patterns for efficient media handling including images, videos, audio, and files in messaging contexts. These principles apply to all media-related operations.

## Best Practices
- Implement progressive loading for all media types
- Design proper caching strategies for different media types
- Support media compression before transmission
- Implement background upload/download with progress reporting
- Design fallback rendering for unsupported media types
- Support pause/resume for large media transfers
- Implement proper media validation before processing
- Design efficient media thumbnail generation
- Support multiple media formats with graceful degradation
- Implement proper media access permissions handling

## File / Project Structure Guidelines
- Organize media-related components:
  ```
  lib/
    core/
      media/
        media_manager.dart
        media_cache.dart
        media_converter.dart
        media_validator.dart
      utils/
        image_processor.dart
        video_processor.dart
        audio_processor.dart
    data/
      repositories/
        media_repository_impl.dart
      datasources/
        media_local_datasource.dart
        media_remote_datasource.dart
    domain/
      repositories/
        media_repository.dart
      entities/
        media_item.dart
        media_attachment.dart
      usecases/
        upload_media_usecase.dart
        process_media_usecase.dart
  ```

## Coding & Styling Conventions
- Use enum for media types: `MediaType.image`, `MediaType.video`
- Implement standardized metadata for media: `MediaMetadata`
- Use factory methods for creating media handlers: `MediaProcessor.forType()`
- Follow consistent naming for media operations: `processImage()`, `processVideo()`
- Define clear interfaces for media processors
- Implement proper error types for media operations
- Document supported formats and limitations

## Performance & Optimization Tips
- Process media in background isolates
- Implement adaptive media quality based on network conditions
- Use efficient compression algorithms appropriate for each media type
- Implement multi-step thumbnailing (quick blur, then actual thumbnail)
- Cache processed media results to avoid reprocessing
- Use memory-efficient media handling libraries
- Implement lazy loading for media galleries
- Pre-process images when appropriate (resize before upload)
- Use hardware acceleration when available
- Implement proper memory management for large media files

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Test media processing with various input formats
- Verify memory consumption during media operations
- Test progressive loading behavior
- Validate cache efficiency and eviction policies
- Test media operations under poor network conditions
- Verify proper handling of corrupted media files
- Test concurrent media operations
- Validate proper cleanup of temporary media files
- Test permissions handling
- Implement performance benchmarks for media operations